       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the safe maximum for metformin.\n\n- **The dose is too high.** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin, and usual single doses are 500\u20131000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n- **A prescriber needs to confirm it.** You said you're not a clinician. A licensed prescriber should place or verify this order, and that applies even if the dose is corrected.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n1. If this was a typo, for example 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg per day) or 1000 mg twice daily, tell me the intended dose. I can enter it with a note that a prescriber verified it.\n2. If the dose is intentional, the treating prescriber should contact pharmacy or order entry directly to document the rationale.\n\nWhat dose did you intend?"
      }
