     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer. The issue isn't whether you meant to write it. The issue is that 5,100 mg per day of metformin is double the labeled maximum and could seriously harm the patient. The order also needs confirmation from a licensed prescriber, and I can't treat a non-clinician's confirmation as that.\n\nHere are the options that would let me proceed:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg per day) or 1000 mg twice daily. The treating prescriber would need to confirm it.\n- **Have the prescriber enter the order.** If they have a clinical reason for an exception, they can place it themselves and work through the pharmacy review and override process.\n\nIf you give me a dose within the labeled range, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
